# Security, Cost & Performance

## Secrets & credentials

- Never hardcode API keys, tokens, or secrets in code, views, JS, or commits.
- Read secrets from `.env` / `config()` only; never expose them to the frontend or logs.
- Do not dump config, env, or request payloads that may contain credentials.

## Billable / third-party APIs

- Treat Maps, Translate, SMS, email, storage, and similar APIs as cost-sensitive.
- Avoid unbounded loops, retries, or bulk calls that can spike usage.
- Prefer caching, batching, and “call only when needed” (on-demand) over eager/always-on requests.
- If a change could increase paid API volume, call it out and confirm before shipping.

## Page speed

- Minimize extra queries, assets, and blocking work on page load.
- Eager-load relationships; avoid N+1 in lists and Livewire renders.
- Prefer lazy-loading images/media and loading heavy JS/CSS only where used.
- Keep Livewire payloads and re-renders small; avoid shipping large unused collections to the view.
- Do not add heavy libraries or unoptimized images without a clear need.
